<section class="cream">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="mission-grid">
      <div class="mission-text">
        <p>
          The Helix Center for Interdisciplinary Investigation was founded in 2012 by
          <strong>{{ site.founder }}</strong>, a psychoanalyst and clinical professor of psychiatry who
          observed how narrow specialization and the grant process were constraining creativity at
          professional scientific meetings. What began as an experiment in
          <span class="highlight">"a university without walls"</span> has grown into one of New York
          City's most distinctive intellectual institutions.
        </p>
        <p>
          Over {{ site.stats.seasons }} seasons, The Helix Center has convened <strong>{{ site.stats.speakers }} distinguished speakers</strong>
          from <strong>{{ site.stats.institutions }} institutions</strong> &mdash; including Columbia, NYU, Princeton, Yale, Harvard,
          MIT, Oxford, Cambridge, and University College London &mdash; for its signature
          <strong>Theaetetus Table</strong> roundtable discussions. These extempore (unscripted)
          conversations bring five experts from different fields together to explore a single question
          at the boundaries of human knowledge.
        </p>
        <p>
          Every event is completely free and open to the public &mdash; an act of intellectual generosity
          made possible by donors who believe in the enduring value of cross-disciplinary inquiry.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="mission-principles">
        <div class="principle">
          <div class="principle-icon">&#8734;</div>
          <div>
            <h4>Interdisciplinary by Design</h4>
            <p>Every roundtable unites voices from multiple fields &mdash; {{ site.stats.disciplines }} disciplines from neuroscience to poetry.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="principle">
          <div class="principle-icon">&#9733;</div>
          <div>
            <h4>Exceptional Caliber</h4>
            <p>{{ site.stats.nobelLaureates }} Nobel laureates, {{ site.stats.macarthurFellows }} MacArthur Fellows, and the most-cited neuroscientist in history.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="principle">
          <div class="principle-icon">&#9881;</div>
          <div>
            <h4>Unrehearsed &amp; Authentic</h4>
            <p>No scripts, no pre-arranged positions. Five scholars sit together and think out loud.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="principle">
          <div class="principle-icon">&#9825;</div>
          <div>
            <h4>Free &amp; Open to All</h4>
            <p>Every event is free. Our entire archive is freely accessible online.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
